# Pickthree licence

Pickthree is proprietary, closed-source software, © Solonex. It is not open source, and nothing in
this repository grants any licence to its source code.

This repository holds only the GitHub Action wrapper: metadata that runs the published Pickthree
container image. You may copy, modify and redistribute the contents of *this repository* freely as
part of using or self-hosting Pickthree.

The software the wrapper runs is licensed, not sold.

**You may** download, install and run the published binaries (the container image, the npm package,
this Action) on infrastructure you control, to review repositories you have access to, within the
limits of your tier — free for public repositories and for private repositories with up to 3
distinct developers per month; larger private use requires a licence file issued by Solonex. All
features are available on every tier; licensing is by size, not by feature.

**You may not** redistribute, sublicense, sell, or offer the software as a hosted service to third
parties; reverse-engineer, modify or remove the licence verification; or circumvent the developer
count.

**No warranty.** The software is provided "as is", without warranty of any kind. Solonex is not
liable for any damages arising from its use. Pickthree sends your code diffs to the LLM provider you
configure with your own credentials; that provider's terms apply to those requests.

Nothing in the software reports usage to Solonex: there is no telemetry and no licence server.
Licences are verified offline.

Full terms: https://pickthree.dev/terms
